        <mxCell id="note1" value="READING THIS: the top lane is what an owner does to stand up a registry, the middle lane is what a gifter does to find and give, the bottom row is the three discovery paths the intended flow asks for. Two facts sit under the whole picture: the app today is one gated link per event circle, not one persistent link per person, and no route in the app is crawlable &#8212; every response carries a noindex header, so &quot;findable by web search&quot; is a change to the privacy posture, not a search feature." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=16;fontColor=#5B5B66;spacing=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
